research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md-349-| G. Festuccia and N. Seiberg, “Rigid Supersymmetric Theories in Curved Superspace,” arXiv:1105.0689v2 (PDF dated 17 May 2011), `https://arxiv.org/pdf/1105.0689` | Retrieved PDF; read the abstract, §1 and §2 general procedure including the auxiliary supergravity backgrounds and gravitino/Killing-spinor equations; inspected the stated S3×R/S3 qualifications. | Not a complete background classification. Their setup assumes the appropriate off-shell supergravity coupling and notes complex auxiliary/background values and reflection-positivity limitations. Each new background needs its own checked Killing-spinor solution. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-localization-bps.md-350-| N. Nekrasov, “Seiberg–Witten Prepotential from Instanton Counting,” hep-th/0206161 (18 Jun 2002), `https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0206161` | Retrieved PDF; read the introduction, §2.2 passages defining equivariant moduli-space integration, §§3.1–3.4 on ADHM, noncompactness/resolution and contour localization, and §4.2's equivariant K-theory/index view. Search hits in §3.5 locate the partition-indexed fixed-point discussion, but the tangent-weight derivation was not read in this pass. | Not a full audit of the gauge-theory path integral or every contour calculation. The paper itself identifies small-instanton and IR noncompactness, uses Ω/noncommutative regularization, and labels the KP/Toda relation conjectural. Instanton count is a formal/equivariant construction under its stated regulator, not a proof of a general continuum path integral. |
