research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-68-| **pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-classical-gauge-invariance** | physics-theorem / physics | From the adopted model and local curvature/gauge formula, prove invariance of the declared classical action or density under the declared gauge group, including boundary conditions. A local density need not be globally a scalar formula in a single trivialization. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-69-| **pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange** | physics-theorem / physics | Vary the global curvature action with compactly supported variations and prove the exact source-free or matter-coupled field equation under the metric and integration conventions. The proof must include the variation \(\delta_A F_A=D_A\delta A\), integration by parts under the stated boundary conditions, and the invariant pairing. Derive any current identity from the matter equations and Bianchi identity; do not cite it as a universal consequence without those hypotheses. |
