research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-111-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-112-Here \(c\) is odd of ghost number \(+1\), \(A\) is even of ghost number \(0\), and \(\rho_*\) is the derivative of the specified representation. Verify the sign of \(sc\) against the selected gauge-action convention; changing \(A^u\) may change signs. Define the differential on every finite jet by commuting it with total derivatives. The nilpotence proof must compute \(s^2c\), \(s^2A\), and \(s^2\psi\), identifying exactly where Lie-algebra Jacobi and the representation identity enter. Then extend to the graded polynomial algebra. An antighost \(\bar c\) and Nakanishi–Lautrup variable \(b\) are a nonminimal contractible pair only after defining \(s\bar c=b,\; sb=0\) and proving the homotopy statement in the same jet algebra. This algebraic cohomology is distinct from physical-state cohomology \(\ker Q_{\mathrm{BRST}}/\operatorname{im}Q_{\mathrm{BRST}}\).
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-113-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:114:For BV, choose a single grading/sign convention and define fields, ghosts, antifields, antibracket, classical master action, and the allowed local functionals. In the irreducible Yang–Mills case the minimal classical master action encodes the classical action, gauge variation term \(A^*D_Ac\), and ghost-antifield term quadratic in \(c\). Prove the master equation and that its Hamiltonian vector field squares to zero by the graded Jacobi identity. State how gauge fixing is represented (for example, a canonical transformation/gauge-fixing fermion or Lagrangian submanifold) and prove only the algebraic claim actually used. Do not equate the classical master equation with a quantum measure or the quantum master equation.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-115-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-116-The existing root BV interface uses a degree-\(+1\) generator, whereas many physics references use a degree-\(-1\) BV Laplacian/bracket convention. Translate every sign, degree and \(\hbar\) power explicitly if those items are consumed. The formal QME is coefficientwise; it does not by itself construct an integral or prove convergence.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-117-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-118-### Perturbative renormalization and anomaly control
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-119-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:120:Keep three mathematical objects separate: formal Feynman coefficients after gauge fixing; locally renormalized time-ordered products/counterterms; and a nonperturbatively defined quantum theory. A perturbative gauge-renormalization item must specify the regularization scheme, gauge parameter, ghosts, matter representation, local counterterm space, ghost number, power counting, and whether the regulator preserves BRST. Prove the Ward/Slavnov–Taylor identity order by order, not by appealing to the scalar causal-extension theorem.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-121-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-122-Local anomalies are classes in the relative local complex \(H^{1,4}(s\mid d_H)\), under a declared finite-jet algebra and locality hypothesis. The Wess–Zumino consistency equation \(s a_4+d_Ha_3=0\) is necessary; exactness means a local counterterm removes the breaking. Show that the relevant obstruction class vanishes for the specified matter representation and regulator before claiming a consistent gauge theory. A semisimple non-Abelian local anomaly, mixed \(U(1)\) anomalies, and global anomalies are distinct. The global \(SU(2)\) anomaly is not detected by a local polynomial in \(H^{1,4}(s\mid d_H)\). The anomaly-matching agent owns the physical representation/defect interface; this gauge scaffold should provide the local complex, not duplicate that output.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-123-
