45:Choose an embedded smooth submanifold \(S\subset X\) of codimension \(k\), a smooth positive density \(\mu_S\), and an open neighborhood \(U\subset X\) of a point \(s\in S\). A **gauge condition** on \(U\) is a smooth map \(\chi:U\to\mathbb R^k\) such that \(U\cap S=\chi^{-1}(0)\) and, for every \(s'\in U\cap S\), \(d\chi_{s'}\) is surjective with kernel \(T_{s'}S\). The **infinitesimal orbit map** at \(s'\) is \(R_{s'}:\mathfrak k\to T_{s'}X\), \(R_{s'}Z=\left.\frac{d}{dt}\right|_{t=0}s'\cdot\exp_K(tZ)\). Its kernel is the Lie algebra of the stabilizer of \(s'\). The **Faddeev–Popov operator** is the ordinary linear map \(M_{s'}:=d\chi_{s'}\circ R_{s'}:\mathfrak k\to\mathbb R^k\). It is **transverse at \(s'\)** when \(M_{s'}\) is an isomorphism, equivalently when \(T_{s'}X=T_{s'}S\oplus\operatorname{im}R_{s'}\). Choose a positive density \(\nu\) on \(\mathfrak k\) equal to \((\mu_K)_e\), and the standard positive density \(\lambda\) on \(\mathbb R^k\). The finite-dimensional Faddeev–Popov Jacobian \(\Delta_{\mathrm{FP}}(s')\) is the nonnegative density ratio defined by \(M_{s'}^*\lambda=\Delta_{\mathrm{FP}}(s')\nu\); in chosen bases it is \(|\det M_{s'}|\), and it is zero when \(M_{s'}\) is singular. A nonzero infinitesimal stabilizer therefore forces a zero Jacobian, while a discrete stabilizer can instead leave a separate finite intersection multiplicity.

