+## Source reading and disposition
+
+Two independent full-text treatments were inspected for the A page, including complete lecture notes:
+
+- David Skinner, Quantum Field Theory II: Advanced Quantum Field Theory lecture notes, chapter “Non-Abelian Gauge Theory: Perturbative Quantization,” https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/AQFT/chap8.pdf, §§8.1–8.1.1, PDF pp. 154–161. The finite-dimensional SO(2) calculation, the transverse derivative, repeated intersections, the stabilizer at the origin, and the explicit warning about the formal continuum measure were inspected. Its functional-integral presentation remains formal; only its finite-dimensional model and scope caveats are harvested.
+- P. K. Mitter and C. M. Viallet, “On the Bundle of Connections and the Gauge Orbit Manifold in Yang–Mills Theory,” Communications in Mathematical Physics 79 (1981), 457–472, full text at https://scispace.com/pdf/on-the-bundle-of-connections-and-the-gauge-orbit-manifold-in-1nks9qpdkj.pdf, §§I–V. The compact connected semisimple matrix group, closed compact oriented Riemannian base, Sobolev order, free based/mod-center action, Coulomb-slice splitting, and inverse-function argument were inspected. It supports the function-space boundary and a local slice in its stated free-action setting; it does not supply a continuum functional measure or the finite proof authored here.
