Choose an embedded smooth submanifold \(S\subset X\) of codimension \(k\), a smooth positive density \(\mu_S\), and an open neighborhood \(U\subset X\) of a point \(s\in S\). Embedded means that near each point of \(S\), a smooth chart on \(X\) identifies \(S\) with \(\mathbb R^{n-k}\times\{0\}\). A **gauge condition** on \(U\) is a smooth map \(\chi:U\to\mathbb R^k\) such that \(U\cap S=\chi^{-1}(0)\) and, for every \(s'\in U\cap S\), \(d\chi_{s'}\) is surjective with kernel \(T_{s'}S\). The **infinitesimal orbit map** at \(s'\) is \(R_{s'}:=d(\alpha_{s'})_e:\mathfrak k\to T_{s'}X\), where \(\alpha_{s'}(g)=s'\cdot g\); call its kernel the infinitesimal stabilizer. The **Faddeev–Popov operator** is the ordinary linear map \(M_{s'}:=d\chi_{s'}\circ R_{s'}:\mathfrak k\to\mathbb R^k\). It is **transverse at \(s'\)** when \(M_{s'}\) is an isomorphism. Choose a positive density \(\nu\) on \(\mathfrak k\) equal to \((\mu_K)_e\), and the standard positive density \(\lambda\) on \(\mathbb R^k\). The finite-dimensional Faddeev–Popov Jacobian \(\Delta_{\mathrm{FP}}(s')\) is the nonnegative density ratio defined by \(M_{s'}^*\lambda=\Delta_{\mathrm{FP}}(s')\nu\); in chosen bases it is \(|\det M_{s'}|\), and it is zero when \(M_{s'}\) is singular.

