# Batch 3 authoring notes — Local Gauge Slices and Faddeev–Popov Jacobians

Run advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23, batch 3 (dependency level 1), owns the A/B pair qftx-gauge-slice-mathematics / qftx-gauge-slice-mathematics-examples.

## Plan and placement

The assigned plan section (research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md, lines 37–56) requires fubini-and-change-of-variables, inverse-and-implicit-function-theorems, and qftx-gauge-geometry. The canonical plan-spec.json records the gauge-geometry page under requires and lists Fubini and inverse-function pages separately under required_source_pages; this is a metadata-shape difference, with the same three required pages. The proposed inventory row in research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json lists only qftx-gauge-geometry in requires. Following the canonical plan and dispatch, the authored A-page frontmatter and batch manifest include all three pages.

The proposed A-page inventory has three planned items: def-qftx-gauge-slice-and-faddeev-popov-operator, thm-qftx-local-faddeev-popov-slice-jacobian, and thm-qftx-singer-global-gauge-section-obstruction. The first two carriers and two B-page worked examples are authored. No Singer theorem carrier is created: the exact hypotheses, configuration/orbit topologies, stabilizer conditions, and proof cannot be recovered from the inspected abstract and introductory lines. The absent carrier and owner escalation are explicit in source coverage below. The A-page frontmatter lists only extant carriers, and both pages have YAML frontmatter only with empty Markdown bodies.

## Items, dependency levels, and conventions

- def-qftx-gauge-slice-and-faddeev-popov-operator (level 2): defines finite-dimensional regulator data (X,K,alpha), a codimension-k slice chi"'^{-1}(0), the orbit derivative, the Faddeev–Popov operator and density ratio. It explicitly separates the regulator action from the full gauge group and makes no continuum determinant or measure claim. Direct in-run suppliers: def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data (level 0), def-qftx-principal-connection-form (level 0), and lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi (level 1). Other exact mathematical premises are recorded in the item metadata.
- thm-qftx-local-faddeev-popov-slice-jacobian (level 3): proves the local orbit-to-slice diffeomorphism and density-normalized Jacobian from the imported inverse function and compactly-supported change-of-variables theorems. Its second clause proves the finite transverse intersection formula with a compactly supported mollifier and distinct slice points. It makes no global-section or continuum-measure claim.
- ex-qftx-translation-gauge-slice-jacobian and ex-qftx-so2-gauge-slice-multiplicity (level 4): explicitly recompute the unit translation Jacobian and the two transverse SO(2) intersections. The SO(2) example verifies that at the origin the stabilizer makes the FP operator singular and the finite-root hypotheses fail.
- A/B page level: 1. The page item inventory remains within the 100-item cap.

The group density is left invariant. For a right action, the tangent to g_i exp(tZ) is d(L_g_i)_e Z; this frame makes the density coefficient constant and identifies the derivative of F_x(g)=chi(x·g) with M_{x·g}. This fixes the density cancellation in the intersection formula. The section-change convention is A'"'=Ad_{u"'^{-1}}A+theta_L(u).

## Current cross-batch evidence

The current batch-2 manifest contains five carriers on qftx-gauge-geometry. loadStep1Record and step1Decision were run against the current run snapshot. They return ready/current for def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data, def-qftx-principal-connection-form, def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket, lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi, and def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative. The three direct item suppliers and page interface were checked against their actual statements and proofs. The cross-batch JSON records one verified row for the page and one for each direct item edge. The form-bracket result is transitive context and is not recorded as an unsupported direct edge.

## Sources and dispositions

1. David Skinner, Quantum Field Theory II: Advanced Quantum Field Theory, full lecture notes, Chapter 8, https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/AQFT/chap8.pdf. Read all of §§8.1–8.1.1, PDF pp. 154–161. Supports the finite SO(2) orbit model, orbit/slice derivative, multiple intersections, stabilizer degeneracy, and warning that the continuum functional integral needs additional assumptions. It is context, not the proof of the local theorem.
2. P. K. Mitter and C. M. Viallet, “On the Bundle of Connections and the Gauge Orbit Manifold in Yang–Mills Theory,” complete 16-page paper read at https://scispace.com/pdf/on-the-bundle-of-connections-and-the-gauge-orbit-manifold-in-1nks9qpdkj.pdf. Read §§I–V, printed pp. 458–472, especially §§IV.B–C, pp. 466–468, and §V, pp. 468–471. Its local slice theorem uses a Sobolev completion, compact connected semisimple matrix group, compact closed oriented Riemannian base, order above dimension/2+1, and free-action/irreducibility conditions. It is not a continuum measure proof and is not imported as the finite theorem'"'s proof. Direct attempt to retrieve the earlier lpthe URL returned 404; the alternate full text was successfully inspected.
3. I. M. Singer, “Some Remarks on the Gribov Ambiguity,” Communications in Mathematical Physics 60 (1978), 7–12, DOI https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01609471. The historical note reports abstract/catalogue and introductory lines only; the full proof and exact hypotheses were not read. Five failures are preserved in batch-3.coverage.json: the historical Project Euclid interstitial, web-open attempts on Project Euclid and a Turin PDF, and curl attempts on Project Euclid (1,158-byte HTML interstitial) and the Turin PDF (403). No sixth attempt was made. The exact redirected Project Euclid URL, Turin PDF URL, attempt times, and exact search-query strings were not retained in the historical note; the coverage record says so rather than guessing. The abstract's broad claim is insufficient to state or prove the assigned theorem. This is an owner escalation; no Singer claim is treated as a proved supplier or as an open problem.

## Current status and next action

The definition, finite-dimensional theorem, examples, A/B frontmatter, manifest, proof-contract file, source-coverage file, and cross-batch dependency array are authored. Current batch-2 direct prerequisites are ready/current. The Singer theorem remains a planned assigned obligation with no carrier and an explicit source/proof escalation. Source-fetch stamping and final scoped checks are pending; record actual outputs here after they run. Per-item Step 1 readiness decisions will be recorded only after the final edits and checks.
