- ex-qftx-translation-gauge-slice-jacobian and ex-qftx-so2-gauge-slice-multiplicity (level 4): explicitly recompute the unit translation Jacobian and the two transverse SO(2) intersections. The SO(2) example verifies that at the origin the stabilizer makes the FP operator singular and the finite-root hypotheses fail.
- A/B page level: 1. The page item inventory remains within the 100-item cap.

The group density is left invariant. For a right action, the tangent to g_i exp(tZ) is d(L_g_i)_e Z; this frame makes the density coefficient constant and identifies the derivative of F_x(g)=chi(x·g) with M_{x·g}. This fixes the density cancellation in the intersection formula. The section-change convention is A'=Ad_{u^{-1}}A+theta_L(u).

## Current cross-batch evidence

The current batch-2 manifest contains five carriers on qftx-gauge-geometry. loadStep1Record and step1Decision were run against the current run snapshot. They return ready/current for def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data, def-qftx-principal-connection-form, def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket, lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi, and def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative. The three direct item suppliers and page interface were checked against their actual statements and proofs. The cross-batch JSON records one verified row for the page and one for each direct item edge. The form-bracket result is transitive context and is not recorded as an unsupported direct edge.

## Sources and dispositions

1. David Skinner, Quantum Field Theory II: Advanced Quantum Field Theory, full lecture notes, Chapter 8, https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/AQFT/chap8.pdf. Read all of §§8.1–8.1.1, PDF pp. 154–161. Supports the finite SO(2) orbit model, orbit/slice derivative, multiple intersections, stabilizer degeneracy, and warning that the continuum functional integral needs additional assumptions. It is context, not the proof of the local theorem.
2. P. K. Mitter and C. M. Viallet, “On the Bundle of Connections and the Gauge Orbit Manifold in Yang–Mills Theory,” complete 16-page paper read at https://scispace.com/pdf/on-the-bundle-of-connections-and-the-gauge-orbit-manifold-in-1nks9qpdkj.pdf. Read §§I–V, printed pp. 458–472, especially §§IV.B–C, pp. 466–468, and §V, pp. 468–471. Its local slice theorem uses a Sobolev completion, compact connected semisimple matrix group, compact closed oriented Riemannian base, order above dimension/2+1, and free-action/irreducibility conditions. It is not a continuum measure proof and is not imported as the finite theorem's proof. Direct attempt to retrieve the earlier lpthe URL returned 404; the alternate full text was successfully inspected via the web PDF view. The required source-fetch-check later returned zero bytes on all five permitted attempts to the cited mirror (after the earlier 404), so it has no fetch_verified stamp. This source remains contextual rather than a proof supplier; the complete finite-dimensional proofs are local. No further fetch attempt will be made.
3. I. M. Singer, “Some Remarks on the Gribov Ambiguity,” Communications in Mathematical Physics 60 (1978), 7–12, DOI https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01609471. The historical note reports abstract/catalogue and introductory lines only; the full proof and exact hypotheses were not read. Five failures are preserved from the initial source-resolution pass: Project Euclid interstitials and two Turin PDF failures. During an unrelated alternative-source search for Mitter–Viallet, a search result surfaced the exact Project Euclid PDF URL https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-60/issue-1/Some-remarks-on-the-Gribov-ambiguity/cmp/1103904019.pdf. Opening it returned a one-line HTML iframe wrapper; a batched screenshot request for its six pages failed because the tool did not resolve an application/pdf document. Those two later failed access routes are also recorded in batch-3.coverage.json. The exact earlier Turin URL and attempt times were not retained in the historical note; the coverage record preserves that uncertainty. The abstract's broad claim is insufficient to state or prove the assigned theorem. This remains an owner escalation; no Singer claim is treated as a proved supplier or as an open problem. No further Singer retrieval attempts will be made.

